[289.85099, "o", "head -n 20 /app/progress.md /app/intrusion-report.md /app/vuln-report.md /app/baseline-report.md /app/remediation-plan.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r==> /app/progress.md <==\r\n# Forensic Investigation Progress & Checklist\r\n\r\n## Incident Overview\r\n- Host: ssh-prod-01 (CentOS 7 Linux)\r\n- Primary Incident Type: SSH Root Brute Force, Monero Cryptomining, Multi-stage Persistence, Anti-Forensics (Log Wiping)\r\n- Status: Investigation & Remediation Planning Complete\r\n\r\n## Timeline of Events (UTC)\r\n1. 2026-08-15 00:53:24 - 00:54:52: External SSH brute-force attack against root user initiated from attacker origin IP `/disk/var/log/secure:141`.\r\n2. 2026-08-15 00:54:55: Attacker successfully authenticates as root via SSH password brute force `/disk/var/log/secure:178`.\r\n3. 2026-08-15 00:55 - 01:29: Attacker conducts post-exploitation activity:\r\n   - Dropped and executed Monero cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n   - Installed cron persistence in `/var/spool/cron/root` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n   - Installed shell-init persistence in `/root/.bashrc` (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).\r\n   - Installed systemd service persistence at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n   - Planted NOPASSWD sudo backdoor in `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).\r\n   - Cleared authentication logs causing log gap between 00:54:55 and 01:29:12 (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\n   - Executed hydra brute-force tool against internal targets from devops user account context (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).\r\n4. 2026-08-15 03:20: Incident detected and intake logged by SOC (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`).\r\n\r\n\r\n==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==\r\n# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nHost `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.\r\n\r\n## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\r\n- **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n- **C2 Beacon Domain:** `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n- **Cryptomining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n- **Monero Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n- **Malware Process PID:** `1337` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\r\n- **Malware Binary Location:** `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`)\r\n- **Malware Binary SHA256 Hash:** `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\r\n\r\n## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis\r\n\r\n### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access\r\nThe attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n\r\n### 2. Execution & Impact (Cryptomining)\r\n\r\n==> /app/vuln-report.md <==\r\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nA comprehensive analysis of vulnerability scan data (`/sas/vulns.json`), threat intelligence advisories (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`), and forensic disk artifacts (`/disk`) was conducted to evaluate whether softwar"]
[289.851031, "o", "e vulnerabilities (CVEs) played any role in the initial compromise of `ssh-prod-01`.\r\n\r\n## Evaluation of Vulnerability Scan Results\r\nThe machine-readable vulnerability scan feed `/sas/vulns.json` contains an empty list (`[]`), indicating that no unpatched software vulnerabilities or active CVE exploits were identified or reported on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\r\n\r\n## Evaluation of Draft Change Ticket Claims (BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708)\r\nThe initial draft change ticket CHG-3182 proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`). \r\n\r\nThis proposal is **FALSE and INCORRECT**:\r\n1. Host `ssh-prod-01` is running CentOS 7 Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`), whereas BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n2. No RDP service or Windows subsystem exists on this Linux host (`/disk/etc/os-release`).\r\n\r\n## True Initial Entry Vector Identification\r\nInitial access was achieved purely through **credential exploitation** (SSH root password brute forcing) rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\r\n- Source IP `198.51.100.78` performed rapid password attempts against port 22 (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`).\r\n- Successful root login occurred at 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC via `Accepted password for root` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\n- Threat intelligence advisory confirms the campaign relies on brute-force SSH logins (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\r\n==> /app/baseline-report.md <==\r\n# Security Baseline and Configuration Analysis Report\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nAnalysis of system configurations on `ssh-prod-01` revealed several severe security baseline deficiencies that directly facilitated the initial breach, enabled privilege escalation, and increased the host's overall attack surface.\r\n\r\n## Baseline Findings & Weaknesses\r\n\r\n### 1. Insecure SSH Configuration (BAS-01 / CHK-04)\r\n- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r\n- **Identified Weaknesses:**\r\n  - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct SSH logins as `root` from remote external hosts (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n  - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password authentication instead of requiring SSH key-based authentication (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n  - `MaxAuthTries 6`: High authentication attempt threshold before disconnection, enabling rapid dictionary brute-forcing (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\r\n- **Security Risk:** Allowed the external attacker at `198.51.100.78` to brute-force the root user password directly over the network (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`).\r\n\r\n### 2. MySQL Remote Root Access and Public Binding (BAS-02 / CHK-09)\r\n- **Artifact Path:** `/etc/my.cnf` (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`)\r\n- **Identified Weaknesses:**\r\n  - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Binds MySQL database service to all network interfaces (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r\n  - Remote root grant enabled: Grants root database privileges over remote network connections (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`).\r\n\r\n==> /app/remediation-plan.md <==\r\n# Comprehensive Post-Incident Remediation & Containment Plan\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nThis remediation plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step procedures to contain the active breach on `ssh-prod-01`, eradicate all persistence mechanisms, harden host baselines, and reconcile the draft change ticket CHG-3182. In accordance with forensic best practices, all actions prioritize backup and quarantine over destructive deletion.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182\r\n\r\nBelow is the updated and corrected change ticket reconciled against forensic evidence in `/disk` and `/sas`:\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Rationale & Evidence |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.78` | PROPOSED | **RECONCILED**: Corrected attacker IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | REJECTED | **RECONCILED**: Rejected BlueK"]
[289.851042, "o", "eep patch claim. Host is CentOS Linux; entry was SSH brute force (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |\r\n| 3 | Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **RECONCILED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Cron persistent beacon on line 5 requires quarantine and removal (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`). |\r\n| 4 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | TODO | **ADDED**: Quarantine and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2 (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`). |\r\n| 5 | Remove systemd persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | TODO | **ADDED**: Disable, stop, and quarantine helper service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). |\r\n| 6 | Remove sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | TODO | **ADDED**: Remove NOPASSWD ALL backdoor entry (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`). |\r\n| 7 | Kill miner process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | TODO | **ADDED**: Terminate process PID 1337 and quarantine binary sample (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). |\r\n"]
